<spell-notebook "textarea theming">
	<header level="1">
		Textarea
		<header>A textarea is a multi-line field used to elicit a longer response.</>
	</>
	<textarea-tab-bar showing="theming"/>
	<section>
		<menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
			<item link="#tokens">Tokens</>
			<item link="#themes">Themes</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- THEMING:  the input family's tokens a textarea reads, live. -->
	<section label="Tokens">
		<markdown>
			A textarea reads the input family's `--ui-input-*` tokens: the shared box, border, colour and placeholder
			tokens, plus its own `--ui-input-textarea-*` (height, its limits, line height). Set one on the element, on any
			ancestor (a form, `:root`), or on the root box through `::part(input)`; style the native `<textarea>` itself
			with `::part(control)`. The [input page](/components/ui/ui-input.html) lists every token of the family.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```css
			ui-textarea {
			  --ui-input-textarea-height: 6em;
			  --ui-input-radius: 0;
			}
			ui-textarea::part(control) {
			  resize: none;
			}
			```
		</>
		<markdown>Edit a value below to try it.</>
		<html>
			<ui-docs-tokens family="ui-input" tokens="--ui-input-textarea* --ui-input-padding* --ui-input-background* --ui-input-color* --ui-input-border* --ui-input-radius --ui-input-placeholder*" playground>
				<ui-textarea fluid placeholder="Type here" aria-label="Preview"></>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Themes">
		<markdown>
			The theme menu above picks the theme for every page of the site:  Spell, Glass, Fruity or Merlot,
			each restyling textareas (the input family's) through its tokens.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
